-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yunus-khan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yunus-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yunus Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yunus Khan was khan of Moghulistan from 1462 to 1487, a Chinggisid ruler of the Chagatai line.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yunus-khoja"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yunus-khoja.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yunus Khoja</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yunus Khoja was the ruler of Tashkent in the late 18th century, who united the city's four rival quarters in the 1780s and built a short-lived independent state.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yunzhong-commandery"><span class="enc-name">Yunzhong Commandery</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Yunzhong Commandery was a frontier commandery of the Qin and Han empires on the northern bend of the Yellow River, near modern Hohhot in Inner Mongolia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yuri Dolgoruky</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri Dolgoruky was Prince of Rostov-Suzdal and, at the end of his life, Grand Prince of Kiev.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-gagarin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-gagarin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yuri Gagarin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri Gagarin was a Soviet pilot and cosmonaut who became the first human in space on 12 April 1961, orbiting the Earth once in Vostok 1, launched from the Baikonur…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-horlis-horsky"><span class="enc-name">Yuri Horlis-Horsky</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri Horlis-Horsky was a Ukrainian officer and writer who fought for the Ukrainian People's Republic and with the insurgents of Kholodny Yar against the Bolsheviks.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-igorevich-of-ryazan"><span class="enc-name">Yuri Igorevich of Ryazan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri Igorevich was Prince of Ryazan when Batu's Mongol army invaded north-eastern Rus' in the winter of 1237.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-boleslav"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-boleslav.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yuri II Boleslav</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri II Boleslav was the last ruler of the Kingdom of Galicia–Volhynia, from 1323 until his death in 1340.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-of-vladimir"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-of-vladimir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yuri II of Vladimir</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri II Vsevolodovich was grand prince of Vladimir from 1212 to 1216 and again from 1218 to 1238, a son of Vsevolod the Big Nest.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-kimimasa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-kimimasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yuri Kimimasa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri Kimimasa was a samurai of the Fukui domain and a financial official of the early Meiji government.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-yaroslavich-of-turov"><span class="enc-name">Yuri Yaroslavich of Turov</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri Yaroslavich was a Rurikid prince, a grandson of Sviatopolk II of Kiev, who established himself in Turov in the late 1150s and resisted attempts by the princes of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuris-day"><span class="enc-name">Yuri's Day</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuri's Day, the autumn feast of St George on 26 November, was the time when Russian peasants were allowed to leave their landlords.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yury-of-moscow"><span class="enc-name">Yury of Moscow</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yury of Moscow was prince of Moscow from 1303 and the first Moscow prince to hold the grand princely throne of Vladimir.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yury-of-zvenigorod"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yury-of-zvenigorod.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yury of Zvenigorod</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yury of Zvenigorod was a son of Dmitry Donskoy and prince of Zvenigorod and Galich.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yury-sviatoslavich"><span class="enc-name">Yury Sviatoslavich</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yury Sviatoslavich was the last independent prince of Smolensk.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yuryev-polsky"><span class="enc-name">Yuryev-Polsky</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Yuryev-Polsky is a small town in Vladimir Oblast, Russia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yushu-tibetan-autonomous-prefecture"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/yushu-tibetan-autonomous-prefecture.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56